<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dónal an Chogaidh Ó Flaithbheartaigh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1565</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Donal of the Battles O'Flaherty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dónal an Chogaidh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oflaherty">Ó Flaithbheartaigh</a>, 'Donal of the Battles', was a chieftain of the O'Flaherty lordship of Iar Connacht in western Ireland and heir to its leadership. He was the first husband of the sea captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grace-omalley">Grace O'Malley</a>, with whom he had three children. He was killed in a feud with a neighbouring family in the 1560s.</p></div>
